# Architecture Boundaries

## Layers and allowed imports
- `src/core`: imports nothing from other layers. No React, Capacitor, DOM, Zustand.
- `src/services`: may import `core`. Only place allowed to touch Capacitor/browser APIs.
- `src/app`: may import `core` and `services` interfaces.
- `src/ui`: may import `app` and only `import type` from `core`.
- `src/main.tsx`: composition root; picks concrete service adapters.

ESLint enforces these rules; do not disable them.

## Determinism
- No `Math.random`, `Date.now`, or I/O in `core`. Inject an `Rng` and timestamps as arguments.

## Side effects
- Reducers and components are pure. Persisting, analytics, ads and haptics happen in app subscribers
  reacting to domain events, or inside services.

```ts
// BAD (inside gameReducer)
storage.save(state)
// GOOD: reducer returns { state, events }; an app subscriber persists on events
```

## Services
- Each platform capability is an interface `XxxService` with adapters such as `capacitor`, `noop`, `memory`.
- The app receives services through `createServices`/providers so tests can inject memory/noop adapters.

## Imports
- Across layers use aliases: `@core/*`, `@app/*`, `@services/*`, `@ui/*`.
- Within the same layer use short relative imports (`./board`). `core` stays alias-free so Node scripts can run it.
